  teach('5.6-08','In a bell the armature is the movable iron strip. Current magnetises the coil core, attracting the strip so the hammer hits the gong and opens the contact. Current then stops, the iron largely demagnetises, and a spring returns the strip and closes the contact. This cycle repeats while the switch is held.')
