 if t==28:
  supp('6.2.5-02','PROC','Plan',8,'Plan a safe coin investigation modelling radioactive half-life. Include equipment, survivor-count measurements, repeats, fixed rules, a results table and the expected graph.','A tray and at least 100 identical coins form the model. The initial count is recorded. The remaining coins are shaken and tossed each round; heads are removed and tails counted. Repeating with the survivors gives a decreasing count. The whole experiment is repeated with the full initial set using the same head-removal rule and tossing method. A table records round number and survivors for each run. Mean survivors plotted against round number should fall by about one half per round, with random variation; one round models the half-life, not a measured time in seconds.',['Equipment/arrangement (1): many identical coins and a tray or contained tossing area.','Measurement (1): initial count recorded.','Procedure (1): toss all remaining coins, remove one specified face and count survivors.','Repetition (1): continue with survivors, then repeat the whole run from the full set.','Controls (1): same removal rule and comparable tossing method.','Safety (1): contain loose coins; keep them away from small children and do not use radioactive material.','Table (1): round number and survivor counts for each run.','Conclusion (1): approximately half survive per round, with fluctuations; identify one-round model half-life. Accept a dice version with correct survival fraction and a fitted half-life rather than assuming one round.'],kind='practical_task')
